  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##Build your Favorites\r\n\r\n**1. Declare the Array -** In `script.js`, declare the favorites array and fill it with at least 3 related string values (e.g., movies, foods).\r\n\r\n**2. Display Indexed Items -** Use `document.getElementById()` and indices `0`, `1`, and `2` to display the first three items of the array into the elements with IDs: `item0`, `item1`, and `item2`.\r\n\r\n**3. Show Total Count -** Use the `.length` property of the array to display the total number of items in the element with the ID count.\r\n\r\n**4. Select and Display One Favorite -** Choose any index (e.g., `1` or `2`) and display that single chosen item into the element with the ID favorite.\r\n\r\n**Success Check:** Your script is working if:\r\n\r\n- Three specific items from your array are visible under \"The First Three.\"\r\n- The total number of favorites is correctly displayed using .length.\r\n- One chosen favorite item is displayed under \"Selected Favorite.\"\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYou may use **AI** to check ID matches, request an example array, or debug \"undefined\" errors,\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
